 ## Background
-Proposal Network Sampling originated from the need to improve importance sampling in Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs). It was introduced in Mip-NeRF 360 [S1], which proposed using a smaller "Proposal Network" MLP to speed up PDF construction while maintaining accuracy. The method is part of a broader class of "PDF Approaches" that directly estimate the PDF along the ray, as opposed to "Spatial Skipping" approaches like Occupancy Grids [S1]. It builds on the concept of transmittance-based importance sampling, where the transmittance estimator is updated through gradient descent during optimization [S1]. Variants include using depth oracle networks for compact representations [S2] and learning sample importance to reduce fine network queries [S6, unofficial].
+Proposal Network Sampling originated from the need to improve importance sampling in Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) [S1]. It was introduced in Mip-NeRF 360 [S1], which proposed using a smaller "Proposal Network" MLP to speed up PDF construction while maintaining accuracy. The method is part of a broader class of "PDF Approaches" that directly estimate the PDF along the ray, as opposed to "Spatial Skipping" approaches like Occupancy Grids [S1]. It builds on the concept of transmittance-based importance sampling, where the transmittance estimator is updated through gradient descent during optimization [S1]. Variants include using depth oracle networks for compact representations [S2] and learning sample importance to reduce fine network queries [S6, unofficial].
 
